🐧 Linux Commands (Basic to Advanced)

📌 1. Basic Navigation Commands
Command          	Definition
pwd	        Show current working directory
ls	        List files and folders
ls -l	      Detailed file list
ls -a	      Show hidden files
cd dir	    Change directory
cd ..	      Move one folder back
cd ~	      Go to home directory
clear	      Clear terminal screen
history	    Show command history

📌 2. File Management Commands

Command	                   Definition
touch file.txt          	Create empty file
cat file.txt	            Display file content
nano file.txt	            Open file editor
vim file.txt	Open Vim editor
cp a b	Copy file
mv a b	Move/Rename file
rm file.txt	Delete file
rm -rf dir	Force delete directory
mkdir dir	Create directory
rmdir dir	Remove empty directory
find / -name file	Search file
locate file	Quickly locate file

📌 3. File Viewing Commands

head file	First 10 lines
tail file	Last 10 lines
tail -f log	Live log monitoring
less file	Read large files
more file	Page-by-page viewing
wc file	Count lines/words
sort file	Sort file contents
uniq file	Remove duplicates
cut -d ":" -f1	Extract columns
awk '{print $1}'	Process text
sed 's/old/new/'	Replace text

📌 4. User Management Commands
Command	Definition
whoami	Current user
id	User and group ID
users	Logged-in users
who	User session details
adduser user	Create user
userdel user	Delete user
passwd user	Change password
groupadd group	Create group
usermod -aG group user	Add user to group
su user	Switch user
sudo command	Run as admin

📌 5. Permission Commands
Command	Definition
chmod 777 file	Change permissions
chmod +x file	Make executable
chown user file	Change owner
chgrp group file	Change group
umask	Default permissions

